{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "38345374",
      "title": "Revisiting Control Structures",
      "sourceHash": "7ede3c081d997adfcdcec2e3695f1e4804c61b7bf3229849e9814fc4a5753dc7",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 3.84,
          "en": "So enough for hobbies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.84,
          "end": 7.71,
          "en": "and objects for now, let's explore control structures.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.71,
          "end": 10.14,
          "en": "I already mentioned the if keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.14,
          "end": 13.86,
          "en": "which is used to create so-called if statements before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.86,
          "end": 18.86,
          "en": "The idea here is that you compare values, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.87,
          "end": 21.48,
          "en": "and you then execute the code inside of the if statement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.48,
          "end": 24.333,
          "en": "only if this condition here is met.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.74,
          "end": 29.61,
          "en": "Now the if statement also allows you to add a else statement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.61,
          "end": 31.8,
          "en": "to define the code that should be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.8,
          "end": 34.47,
          "en": "if this condition is not met.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.47,
          "end": 36.93,
          "en": "And also else if statements if you want check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.93,
          "end": 39.933,
          "en": "for more conditions if the first condition wasn't met.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.83,
          "end": 45.33,
          "en": "And you can add as many else if statements here as you want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.33,
          "end": 47.733,
          "en": "but only one else branch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.32,
          "end": 52.14,
          "en": "Now of course, checking for hard-coded values like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.14,
          "end": 53.79,
          "en": "makes absolutely no sense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.79,
          "end": 56.76,
          "en": "This will always be true, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.76,
          "end": 59.55,
          "en": "Instead, typically, of course, you'll use if statements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.55,
          "end": 63.15,
          "en": "to check content you don't know in advance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.15,
          "end": 66.96,
          "en": "For example, here I could get some dummy password",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.96,
          "end": 69.9,
          "en": "by using the built-in prompt function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.9,
          "end": 72.18,
          "en": "This is a function provided by the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.18,
          "end": 74.583,
          "en": "which will prompt the user for input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.05,
          "end": 78.78,
          "en": "You see here I get this overlay that opens up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.78,
          "end": 81.3,
          "en": "Here I could type your password,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.3,
          "end": 83.31,
          "en": "and now I would get this overlay",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.31,
          "end": 84.993,
          "en": "which asks me for a password.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.31,
          "end": 87.96000000000001,
          "en": "Now here I'm getting this overlay",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.96000000000001,
          "end": 91.11,
          "en": "whenever I type a couple of characters in my code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.11,
          "end": 92.97,
          "en": "and since this is a bit annoying,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.97,
          "end": 97.97,
          "en": "I'll indeed go to the preferences here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.13,
          "end": 100.09,
          "en": "and then the CodeSandbox settings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 102.66,
          "end": 107.37,
          "en": "and set the preview settings to disable preview on edit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 107.37,
          "end": 110.85,
          "en": "so that it will not automatically re-execute the code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.85,
          "end": 112.863,
          "en": "after I typed a couple of characters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 114.53999999999999,
          "end": 116.78999999999999,
          "en": "So with that, I'm now fetching this password,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.78999999999999,
          "end": 120.99,
          "en": "and I could now check if the password is equal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 120.99,
          "end": 122.13,
          "en": "using the triple equals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.13,
          "end": 126.903,
          "en": "and operator to hello, let's say, written like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 128.07,
          "end": 133.07,
          "en": "And if that's the case, I'll console log, hello works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 134.46,
          "end": 137.94,
          "en": "else, if this condition here should not be met,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 137.94,
          "end": 140.76,
          "en": "if the password entered by the user is not hello,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 140.76,
          "end": 141.81,
          "en": "written like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 141.81,
          "end": 145.38,
          "en": "I could check if the password is maybe equal to hello,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 145.38,
          "end": 147.513,
          "en": "starting with a lowercase L,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 148.35,
          "end": 153.09300000000002,
          "en": "in which case, here, I could console log hello works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 154.68,
          "end": 156.93,
          "en": "But also, if that's also not the case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 156.93,
          "end": 159.9,
          "en": "I might want to execute this fallback code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 159.9,
          "end": 163.023,
          "en": "where I say access not granted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 165.21,
          "end": 167.01,
          "en": "With this, now if I save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 167.01,
          "end": 169.26,
          "en": "the code does get executed again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 169.26,
          "end": 170.4,
          "en": "but I'll still cancel this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 170.4,
          "end": 173.94,
          "en": "and manually refresh to clear the console.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 173.94,
          "end": 178.11,
          "en": "And now if I enter hello with a capital L,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 178.11,
          "end": 182.22,
          "en": "and press okay in my console, I'll see hello works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 182.22,
          "end": 185.52,
          "en": "because since I entered hello, written like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 185.52,
          "end": 190.173,
          "en": "this condition here was met and this code here was executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 191.31,
          "end": 196.11,
          "en": "On the other hand, this code and this code was not executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 196.11,
          "end": 199.26,
          "en": "That's why the if statement is called a control structure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 199.26,
          "end": 201.933,
          "en": "because it controls which code gets executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 203.13,
          "end": 205.07999999999998,
          "en": "If I reload this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 205.07999999999998,
          "end": 207.78,
          "en": "and I enter anything else like this here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 207.78,
          "end": 211.71,
          "en": "and I press okay, I get access not granted,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 211.71,
          "end": 213.84,
          "en": "because of course I didn't never enter hello",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 213.84,
          "end": 216.15,
          "en": "written like this nor written like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 216.15,
          "end": 218.673,
          "en": "Therefore, this code got executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 219.81,
          "end": 221.79,
          "en": "So that's the if statement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 221.79,
          "end": 223.74,
          "en": "Another crucial control structure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 223.74,
          "end": 226.5,
          "en": "you should know about is the for loop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 226.5,
          "end": 230.19,
          "en": "Now JavaScript knows different types of for loops,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 230.19,
          "end": 232.59,
          "en": "one very important kind of for loop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 232.59,
          "end": 235.71,
          "en": "we'll also see in this course is the for loop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 235.71,
          "end": 238.233,
          "en": "where we loop through an array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 239.34,
          "end": 243.39,
          "en": "For that, I'll again create my hobbies dummy array here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 243.39,
          "end": 246.63,
          "en": "with sports and cooking, let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 246.63,
          "end": 248.73,
          "en": "and now if I want to execute some code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 248.73,
          "end": 251.04,
          "en": "for every entry in this array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 251.04,
          "end": 254.91,
          "en": "I could create a for loop where I create a constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 254.91,
          "end": 259.2,
          "en": "that will be recreated for every iteration of that for loop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 259.2,
          "end": 261.75,
          "en": "because for loops are about executing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 261.75,
          "end": 265.74,
          "en": "the same piece of code multiple times, as you will see.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 265.74,
          "end": 268.2,
          "en": "And I could name this constant, hobby,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 268.2,
          "end": 270.6,
          "en": "because now with the special of keyword,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 270.6,
          "end": 274.23,
          "en": "I tell JavaScript that it should create a new constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 274.23,
          "end": 276.63,
          "en": "for every item in this array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 276.63,
          "end": 278.13,
          "en": "and it should execute the code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 278.13,
          "end": 281.1,
          "en": "between these curly braces as often as needed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 281.1,
          "end": 284.37,
          "en": "to go through all these elements in this array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 284.37,
          "end": 287.25,
          "en": "so for this array, two times.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 287.25,
          "end": 290.4,
          "en": "So if I then console log hobby here, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 290.4,
          "end": 295.4,
          "en": "this code, this console log code will get executed twice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 295.47,
          "end": 297.9,
          "en": "because I have two elements in this array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 297.9,
          "end": 301.05,
          "en": "The first time for hobby being equal to sports,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 301.05,
          "end": 303.903,
          "en": "the second time for hobby being equal to cooking.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 305.1,
          "end": 307.44,
          "en": "If I save this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 307.44,
          "end": 309.93,
          "en": "and I reload here, enter anything here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 309.93,
          "end": 312.63,
          "en": "and open the console, I see sports",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 312.63,
          "end": 314.16,
          "en": "and cooking being output here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 314.16,
          "end": 318.513,
          "en": "because of this line of code being executed multiple times.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 319.68,
          "end": 323.19,
          "en": "So this for of loop is also a kind of loop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 323.19,
          "end": 324.48,
          "en": "you should be aware of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 324.48,
          "end": 326.823,
          "en": "because we'll also see this in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}